  "details": "I understand that the reasoning for slowing down image/video/text load requests is probably to prevent their requests from passing information out to external servers at a useful rate, since loads can be triggered programmatically in a meaningful order.\n\nHowever:  if there were an \"always load the following list of urls automatically on world launch\" feature, this would not pose that threat;  the VRChat client would guarantee that exactly the same requests are fired every time, so no 'per-session' data could possibly be gleaned from this.\n\nThis would then allow us to have things like image galleries, or multiple configuration files, which are available (almost) immediately on world load, rather than waiting entire minutes for them to finish.   Any *dynamic* loads could still be beholden to the 5-second rule for security reasons, but all the content that's meant to be loaded up front could be ready much quicker with no security downsides.",
